  "title": "Spiking activity (MUA) and LFP from two microwires in human V2/V3, one patient, stimulus-locked epochs of 7 visual experiments (Self et al. 2016; derivative)",
  "description": "Stimulus-locked epochs of multi-unit activity (MUA) and local field potentials (LFP) recorded from two microwires in human early visual cortex (V2/V3) of a single epilepsy patient. The data cover seven visual experiments: receptive field mapping, orientation, spatial frequency, contrast and size tuning, contextual modulation, and curve tracing. This is a BIDS iEEG derivative repackaging of the OSF deposit accompanying Self et al. 2016.",
  "methods_description": "Microwire recordings were made at 32.5 kHz with a NeuraLynx HS-9 head-stage and re-referenced to the average of other microwires. LFP (1-200 Hz), MUA envelope (500 Hz-5 kHz) and thresholded MUA were derived at about 930 Hz and epoched around stimulus onset. Visual stimuli were shown on an LCD with fixation enforced by eye tracking (EyeLink, 1000 Hz).",
